accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  finaltype  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  05 removed_month 94 accessioned on  05 removed_month 94 at 16 43 clinical data  48 year old female post menopausal who had a palpable breast mass in removed_month at which time she was on premarin  no palpable lymphadenopathy  on exam  solid lesion at 10 o clock lateral to areola  on ultrasound solid lesion  now for excisional biopsy of right breast                                                                                      final diagnosis     breast  right   excision   infiltrating ductal carcinoma  80     moderately to poorly differentiated  grade 3 3    ductal carcinoma in situ  20      see note   note  the infiltrating carcinoma measures 1 8cm in greatest dimension and is present at several surgical resection margins  er and pr receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  no lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  the gross frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  diagnosis by  michael pins  m d  signed on  13 removed_month 94 at 16 50                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  right   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  19 removed_month 94 at 08 20 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a 2 x removed_date x 1 4cm tan red  yellow fragment of fibroadipose tissue  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal one small focus of borderline suspicion that is too small for frozen section analysis  the specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes a through d  resident  ross c  wheeler  md                                                                                 source care unit  surgical day care   acc 3 reports to  susan e briggs  m d  martha elizabeth meaney  m d  part   breast mass  right    report_end  , Present.
